window.MOCK_PAPER = {"title": "Exam 2 - PawPrint Dog Boarding", "subtitle": "A second full exam-format paper: a dog-boarding scenario with a Create boarding use case (create, loop and alt frames), a kiosk usability critique, a Loop partial DSD, ADO.NET code tracing and a summary report.", "summary": "100 marks &middot; 3 sections &middot; 3 hours (exam format).", "duration": 180, "sections": [{"key": "A", "title": "Section A - Multiple Choice Questions", "marks": 15, "color": "blue", "time": "about 40 minutes", "parts": [{"type": "mcq", "heading": "A - Multiple choice, Blocks 3 &amp; 4 (15 marks)", "start": 1, "intro": "Answer all 30 questions. Each question carries &frac12; mark (15 marks in total). The questions test reasoning and analytical skills rather than recall: you will diagnose a design, trace code, choose between competing options and justify the choice. Read every option before answering, because several are plausible. Topics: the relational model, keys and integrity rules; normalisation and anomalies; data types and storage; the three-layer architecture and DSD frames; ADO.NET, C# controls and usability frameworks.", "items": [["DOG(DogID, DogName, OwnerID) has OwnerID as a foreign key to OWNER, which holds owners 77 and 78. A clerk edits dog 5 and changes its OwnerID from 77 to 99. What happens, and which rule applies?", ["The update is accepted, because OwnerID is not part of the primary key of DOG, so no rule applies", "The update is accepted and owner 99 is created automatically in OWNER by the DBMS", "The update is rejected by entity integrity, because the value of a key column was changed", "The update is rejected: no owner 99 exists, so the dog would be an orphan (referential integrity)"], 3, "A foreign key value must match an existing primary key value, or be NULL. Changing a foreign key to a value with no parent breaks that rule just like an insert would."], ["OWNER holds owners 77 and 78. DOG holds (DogID, OwnerID): (1, 77), (2, 77), (3, NULL), (4, 79), (5, 78), and OwnerID allows NULL. Which dogs violate referential integrity?", ["Only dog 4", "Dogs 3 and 4", "Dogs 1 and 2, because owner 77 repeats", "Dogs 2 and 3"], 0, "A foreign key value may repeat (many dogs per owner) and may be NULL if the column allows it. Only dog 4 refers to an owner (79) that does not exist."], ["BOARDING_SERVICE has the composite primary key (BoardingNo, ServiceCode) and holds (101, GR). Which row can <b>not</b> be inserted next?", ["(101, WK)", "(102, GR)", "(103, WK)", "(101, GR) again, with a different Qty"], 3, "The <i>combination</i> must be unique. (101, WK) and (102, GR) re-use one value but form new combinations. A different Qty does not matter, because Qty is not part of the key.", "<div class=\"diagram-wrap\"><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 94\" width=\"320\" height=\"94\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"BOARDING_SERVICE with one row and a composite primary key\"><defs><marker id=\"f5\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"o5\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker><marker id=\"b5\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#1a56c4\"/></marker><marker id=\"r5\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#b3261e\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"94\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BOARDING_SERVICE</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"34\" width=\"270\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"70.0\" y=\"49\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\">BoardingNo</text><text x=\"170.0\" y=\"49\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\">ServiceCode</text><text x=\"255.0\" y=\"49\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Qty</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"56\" width=\"270\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"70.0\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">101</text><text x=\"170.0\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">GR</text><text x=\"255.0\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">1</text><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"34\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"78\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><line x1=\"220\" y1=\"34\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"78\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/></svg></div>"], ["Business rule: <i>a kennel can hold many boardings over time, and each boarding takes place in exactly one kennel</i>. Where does the foreign key go?", ["KENNEL gets a BoardingNo column", "BOARDING gets a KennelNo column", "A third table is always needed", "Both tables get a foreign key to each other"], 1, "In a one-to-many relationship the primary key of the &lsquo;one&rsquo; side (KENNEL) is copied into the &lsquo;many&rsquo; side (BOARDING) as a foreign key.", "<div class=\"diagram-wrap\"><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 560 80\" width=\"560\" height=\"80\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Class diagram: KENNEL to BOARDING\"><defs><marker id=\"f6\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"o6\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker><marker id=\"b6\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#1a56c4\"/></marker><marker id=\"r6\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#b3261e\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"560\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#fff\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"16\" width=\"170\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"16\" width=\"170\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"105.0\" y=\"33\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">KENNEL</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">KennelNo</text><rect x=\"370\" y=\"16\" width=\"170\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"370\" y=\"16\" width=\"170\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"455.0\" y=\"33\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BOARDING</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BoardingNo</text><line x1=\"190\" y1=\"41.0\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"41.0\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"196\" y=\"35.0\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1a56c4\">1..1</text><text x=\"364\" y=\"35.0\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1a56c4\">0..*</text><text x=\"280.0\" y=\"35.0\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#6b7686\" font-style=\"italic\">holds</text></svg></div>"], ["BOARDING_SHEET(<u>BoardingNo, ServiceCode</u>, ServiceName, Qty). ServiceCode &rarr; ServiceName. Assuming all values are atomic, what is the highest normal form of the table?", ["Unnormalised", "3NF", "2NF", "1NF"], 3, "ServiceName depends on only part of the composite key (ServiceCode): a partial dependency, so 2NF is violated and the table is in 1NF only."], ["OWNER(<u>OwnerID</u>, OwnerName, SuburbCode, SuburbName). SuburbCode &rarr; SuburbName. Which problem does this design cause?", ["OwnerID values will be duplicated for every owner who lives in the same suburb", "An owner can have only one suburb, so owners who move cannot be stored", "A new suburb cannot be stored until an owner lives in it (insertion anomaly)", "The table violates 2NF because of a partial dependency"], 2, "SuburbName is determined by a non-key attribute: a transitive dependency (3NF violation). Because the key is a single column, a partial dependency is impossible, so 2NF is satisfied."], ["The primary key of BOARDING_SERVICE is (BoardingNo, ServiceCode). Which dependency is a <b>partial</b> dependency?", ["(BoardingNo, ServiceCode) &rarr; Qty", "CheckInDate &rarr; BoardingNo", "BoardingNo &rarr; CheckInDate", "Qty &rarr; ServiceCode"], 2, "A partial dependency is a non-key attribute depending on <i>part</i> of the key. BoardingNo alone determines CheckInDate. Qty depends on the whole key, a full dependency.", "<div class=\"diagram-wrap\"><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 432 110\" width=\"432\" height=\"110\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Functional dependency diagram for BOARDING_SERVICE\"><defs><marker id=\"f7\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"o7\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker><marker id=\"b7\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#1a56c4\"/></marker><marker id=\"r7\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#b3261e\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"432\" height=\"110\" fill=\"#fff\"/><rect x=\"14\" y=\"14\" width=\"90.0\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"59.0\" y=\"33\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\">BoardingNo</text><rect x=\"130.0\" y=\"14\" width=\"96.8\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"178.4\" y=\"33\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\">ServiceCode</text><rect x=\"252.8\" y=\"14\" width=\"96.8\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"301.2\" y=\"33\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">CheckInDate</text><rect x=\"375.6\" y=\"14\" width=\"42.4\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"396.8\" y=\"33\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Qty</text><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"62\" x2=\"301.2\" y2=\"62\" stroke=\"#1a56c4\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"42\" x2=\"59.0\" y2=\"62\" stroke=\"#1a56c4\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"301.2\" y1=\"62\" x2=\"301.2\" y2=\"43\" stroke=\"#1a56c4\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#b7)\"/><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"82\" x2=\"396.8\" y2=\"82\" stroke=\"#1a56c4\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"42\" x2=\"59.0\" y2=\"82\" stroke=\"#1a56c4\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"178.4\" y1=\"42\" x2=\"178.4\" y2=\"82\" stroke=\"#1a56c4\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"396.8\" y1=\"82\" x2=\"396.8\" y2=\"43\" stroke=\"#1a56c4\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#b7)\"/></svg></div>"], ["DOG.NightsStayed is declared as a Byte field (whole numbers 0 to 255). A long-stay dog has now boarded 270 nights and the clerk saves the update. What is the most likely outcome and the best fix?", ["The value is accepted and quietly rounded down to 255, so no error appears and nothing is lost", "The value wraps around to 14 when saved, so nothing needs to be done about it", "The update is rejected, because the type cannot hold 270; change the field size to Integer", "Access converts the column to Long Text automatically so that the value fits"], 2, "A data type fixes the range of values a column can hold. 270 is outside 0 to 255, so the save fails. Integer (up to 32,767) is the smallest size that fits, which keeps the storage economical."], ["The DOG table has a column <code class=\"inline\">Vaccinations</code> containing &lsquo;Rabies, Parvo, Distemper&rsquo;. What is the best fix?", ["Make the column wider so that the whole list of vaccinations fits in it", "Add columns Vaccination1, Vaccination2 and Vaccination3 to DOG", "Create a VACCINATION table with a DogID foreign key and one row per vaccination", "Store the list in a memo field so that the text can be as long as needed"], 2, "A multi-valued attribute breaks 1NF. A repeating group of extra columns (Vaccination1, Vaccination2, &hellip;) is still poor design. A child table in a one-to-many relationship allows any number of vaccinations."], ["A dog&rsquo;s medicine dose is calculated as 0.5 mg per kg. DogWeightKg is declared as a whole-number type and a 12.5 kg dog is saved. What is the likely effect?", ["The weight is rounded to a whole number, so doses are slightly wrong; use a decimal type", "Nothing: a whole-number type stores 12.5 exactly, so the dose calculation is not affected", "The save is rejected, because whole-number types cannot store a value with digits after the point", "The value is stored as text, so no dose can be calculated from it at all"], 0, "The data type limits what can be stored. A whole-number type cannot keep the .5, so the weight is rounded and every calculation based on it is affected."], ["DogName is declared <code>VARCHAR(30)</code>. A clerk types a 35-character registered name. What is the expected result?", ["It is stored in full, because VARCHAR has no limit on how many characters it can hold", "It does not fit the maximum of 30, so it is rejected or must be shortened", "It is stored in full and every row&rsquo;s column grows to 35 characters", "The extra 5 characters are saved in a second table that the DBMS creates for overflow"], 1, "The number in VARCHAR(n) is a maximum length. It does not reserve space, but it also cannot be exceeded."], ["The kennel adds four columns to DOG. Which pair should be stored as Yes/No fields?", ["Age and WeightKg", "Size (small / medium / large) and Temperament (calm / nervous / aggressive)", "IsNeutered and NeedsMedication", "IsNeutered and FavouriteToy"], 2, "Yes/No suits attributes with exactly two possible values. Size and temperament have three, age and weight are measurements, and a favourite toy is free text."], ["After 2,000 vaccination certificates (about 1 MB each) are stored inside the dog records, the Access file is over 2 GB and can no longer grow. Which design change best fixes this?", ["Split DOG into two tables with 1,000 dogs each, so each file holds half the PDFs", "Change the column to Long Text, because the PDFs compress when stored as text", "Change DogID from AutoNumber to Long Integer so that it can address more data", "Keep the PDFs in a folder and store only their paths as Short Text in the table"], 3, "Binary files make the database file grow very quickly, and an Access file has a 2 GB limit. Storing paths keeps the table small. Changing column types or splitting rows does not reduce the files&rsquo; size."], ["Flow of activities for <i>Create boarding</i>: 1 the receptionist enters the dog&rsquo;s ID; 2 the system finds the dog; 3 the receptionist picks a kennel; 4 the system checks that the kennel is free; 5 the system creates the boarding. Which lifelines does the DSD need, apart from the new boarding?", [":CreateBoardingForm, :boardingHandler, :Dog, :Kennel", ":CreateBoardingForm, :Dog, :Kennel", ":Receptionist, :boardingHandler, :Boarding, :Kennel", ":CreateBoardingForm, :boardingHandler, :Dog, :Kennel, :Receptionist"], 0, "The DSD needs the boundary, the controller and one entity for each thing the steps read or check (Dog and Kennel). The new Boarding is drawn when it is created. The actor is not a lifeline."], ["In a DSD, <code>getSelectedServices()</code> (which returns the owner&rsquo;s 4 selected services) is drawn inside <code>loop [for each selected service]</code> together with <code>reserveService()</code>. What is wrong?", ["Nothing is wrong: every message of the use case must sit inside the loop frame, in order", "getSelectedServices() is sent 4 times; send it once before the loop, keep only reserveService() in", "The loop should be an opt frame, because the services that are selected are optional", "reserveService() should be drawn outside the loop, together with the other messages"], 1, "Only the messages that must repeat for each item belong inside the loop. The list is fetched once and then processed item by item."], ["A DSD contains <code class=\"inline\">loop [for each service]</code> enclosing <code class=\"inline\">opt [service is in stock]</code> and the message <code class=\"inline\">reserveService()</code>. There are 4 services, of which 3 are in stock. How many times is the guard evaluated and the message sent?", ["Guard 3 times, message 3 times", "Guard 4 times, message 3 times", "Guard once, message 3 times", "Guard 4 times, message 4 times"], 1, "The loop body runs for every service (4), so the opt guard is tested 4 times; the message inside is sent only when the guard is true (3 times).", "<div class=\"diagram-wrap\"><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 214\" width=\"600\" height=\"214\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Sequence diagram with a loop frame containing an opt frame\"><defs><marker id=\"f8\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"o8\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker><marker id=\"b8\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#1a56c4\"/></marker><marker id=\"r8\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#b3261e\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"600\" height=\"214\" fill=\"#fff\"/><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"36\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"208\" stroke=\"#6b7686\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"36\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"208\" stroke=\"#6b7686\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><line x1=\"490\" y1=\"36\" x2=\"490\" y2=\"208\" stroke=\"#6b7686\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><rect x=\"54.5\" y=\"10\" width=\"111\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">:BoardingForm</text><rect x=\"234.0\" y=\"10\" width=\"132\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">:boardingHandler</text><rect x=\"452.0\" y=\"10\" width=\"76\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"490\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">:Service</text><rect x=\"262\" y=\"114\" width=\"266\" height=\"68\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><rect x=\"262\" y=\"114\" width=\"35\" height=\"17\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"279.5\" y=\"126.5\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">opt</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"127\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">[service is in stock]</text><rect x=\"252\" y=\"86\" width=\"286\" height=\"106\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><rect x=\"252\" y=\"86\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"273.0\" y=\"98.5\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">loop</text><text x=\"302\" y=\"99\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">[for each service]</text><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"64\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" marker-end=\"url(#f8)\"/><text x=\"205.0\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">selectServices()</text><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"154\" x2=\"490\" y2=\"154\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" marker-end=\"url(#f8)\"/><text x=\"395.0\" y=\"149\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">reserveService()</text></svg></div>"], ["<i>Create boarding</i> uses a ref frame named <i>Search dog</i>. Later the Search dog use case gets an extra step: &lsquo;the system checks that the dog is not blacklisted&rsquo;. Which DSDs must be redrawn?", ["Neither, because DSDs are not affected by use case changes", "Both, because the ref frame holds a copy of the messages", "Only Create boarding, because it uses Search dog", "Only the Search dog DSD; Create boarding keeps its ref frame unchanged"], 3, "A ref frame points to another diagram instead of copying it, so a change is made once in the referenced DSD."], ["<code>cmd.ExecuteReader()</code> returns two rows, and the code immediately reads <code>rdr[&quot;DogName&quot;]</code> without calling <code>Read()</code>. What happens?", ["An InvalidOperationException: the reader sits before row one until Read() is called", "The name of the first row is returned, because the reader starts on row one", "null is returned, because no row has been selected by the reader yet at that point", "The names of both rows are returned together as an array of strings from the reader"], 0, "A data reader starts positioned before the first row. Each call to Read() advances to the next row and returns false when there are no more."], ["The kiosk clears all 12 fields when the check-out date is mistyped. Which redesign best offers simple error handling?", ["Show a longer error message that lists every field on the form, but keep clearing them", "Keep the other 11 values, mark only the date field and show the expected format", "Disable the Submit button for the rest of the session once any error has been made", "Replace the date field with a text note"], 1, "Error handling should be simple and local: point at the problem, say how to fix it, and keep everything the user entered correctly."], ["<code>SELECT ServicePrice, ServiceName FROM SERVICE WHERE ServiceCode = ?</code> matches one row and is run with <code>ExecuteScalar()</code>. What is returned?", ["The ServiceName, because it is the last column", "A two-item array holding the price and the name", "Only the ServicePrice value, the first column of the first row", "An OleDbException, because two columns were selected"], 2, "ExecuteScalar returns the first column of the first row and ignores everything else. No error is raised."], ["The boarding kiosk forces owners through nine screens in a fixed order, moves on by itself after 10 seconds, and logs the owner out while a form is half filled. Which change gives owners the most control?", ["Play a warning sound before each automatic logout, so that owners can react in time", "Shorten the automatic advance to 5 seconds, so that owners finish the screens sooner", "Add a progress bar that shows how many of the nine screens remain, but change nothing else", "Let owners go back and forward, advance only on Next, and keep entries after a timeout"], 3, "Supporting an internal locus of control means the user starts and directs the actions. A progress bar or a faster timer does not change who is in control."], ["<code>INSERT INTO BOARDING (BoardingNo, DogID, KennelNo) VALUES (?, ?, ?)</code> is run after only two parameters have been added to the command. What happens?", ["An OleDbException is raised (a required parameter has no value); nothing is inserted", "A row is inserted with KennelNo set to NULL, because the third parameter is missing", "The last parameter is reused for the missing one, so the row is inserted anyway", "The code fails to compile, because the number of parameters is checked by the compiler"], 0, "Parameters are matched by position and each ? needs a value. A missing one is detected when the command runs, not at compile time."], ["The designer wants to apply &lsquo;aesthetic and minimalist design&rsquo; to the kiosk screen in the figure. Which set of changes does so without removing information the task needs?", ["Delete the check-in and check-out fields, because 14 fields are far too many for one screen", "Remove the flashing banner, use one font, and hide rare fields behind 'More details'", "Keep every field but make the promotion banner bigger so that owners notice the offer", "Add a help window that explains each of the 14 fields, and keep everything else as it is"], 1, "Minimalist design removes what is irrelevant or distracting while keeping what the task requires. Deleting the date fields breaks the task, and a bigger banner or an extra window adds clutter.", "<div class=\"diagram-wrap\"><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 580 350\" width=\"580\" height=\"350\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Kiosk screen with 14 fields, a promotion banner and three fonts\"><defs><marker id=\"f10\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"o10\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker><marker id=\"b10\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#1a56c4\"/></marker><marker id=\"r10\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#b3261e\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"580\" height=\"350\" fill=\"#fff\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"560\" height=\"330\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"560\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Kiosk - Boarding</text><text x=\"558\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">&#10005;</text><rect x=\"11\" y=\"35\" width=\"558\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#fff6d6\" stroke=\"#e8c26a\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"290\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#b45f00\">&#9733; SALE!!! 50% OFF ALL STAYS &#9733;  (flashing)</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif\">Owner name</text><rect x=\"129.0\" y=\"72\" width=\"145.0\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" style=\"font-family:Courier New,monospace\">Surname</text><rect x=\"129.0\" y=\"108\" width=\"145.0\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS,cursive\">Phone</text><rect x=\"129.0\" y=\"144\" width=\"145.0\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif\">E-mail</text><rect x=\"129.0\" y=\"180\" width=\"145.0\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" style=\"font-family:Courier New,monospace\">Dog name</text><rect x=\"129.0\" y=\"216\" width=\"145.0\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS,cursive\">Breed</text><rect x=\"129.0\" y=\"252\" width=\"145.0\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"302\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif\">Age</text><rect x=\"129.0\" y=\"288\" width=\"145.0\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"294\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" style=\"font-family:Courier New,monospace\">Weight</text><rect x=\"399.0\" y=\"72\" width=\"145.0\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"294\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS,cursive\">Kennel</text><rect x=\"399.0\" y=\"108\" width=\"145.0\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"294\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif\">Check-in</text><rect x=\"399.0\" y=\"144\" width=\"145.0\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"294\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" style=\"font-family:Courier New,monospace\">Check-out</text><rect x=\"399.0\" y=\"180\" width=\"145.0\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"294\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS,cursive\">Services</text><rect x=\"399.0\" y=\"216\" width=\"145.0\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"294\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif\">Vet name</text><rect x=\"399.0\" y=\"252\" width=\"145.0\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"294\" y=\"302\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" style=\"font-family:Courier New,monospace\">Notes</text><rect x=\"399.0\" y=\"288\" width=\"145.0\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1\"/></svg></div>"], ["Owners must remember the kennel code from an earlier screen and type it in later. Which change best reduces short-term memory load?", ["Make the code field longer, so that it is easier to find and type on the later screen", "Ask owners to write the code on paper, so that they can copy it later", "Show the kennel's name and code on later screens, and let owners pick it from a list", "Show the code once for five seconds on the first screen, before it disappears"], 2, "Shneiderman&rsquo;s rule is to keep displays simple and avoid making users hold information in their heads. Showing it where it is needed and letting users choose removes the recall."], ["At the kennel kiosk, owners tap <i>Cancel boarding</i> expecting the deposit to be refunded automatically, because on every other booking site cancelling means a refund. The kiosk only changes the booking status and the refund is a separate manual process, so owners phone the front desk. Which usability concept best explains the problem?", ["The screen is inconsistent with other screens of the same application", "The system model does not match the user&rsquo;s mental model", "The system gives no feedback after the button is pressed", "The button is not a signifier of an action"], 1, "Users form expectations from past experience. When the system behaves differently, the mental model and the system model do not match. The kiosk is internally consistent, the button is clearly clickable, and the failure is about what the action does."], ["<code class=\"inline\">DOG(<u>DogID</u>, MicrochipNo, DogName, Breed, OwnerID)</code>: both <code class=\"inline\">DogID</code> and <code class=\"inline\">MicrochipNo</code> are unique for every dog, and DogID was chosen as the primary key. Which statement is correct?", ["{DogID, DogName} is a superkey but not a candidate key, because DogName can be removed", "{DogID, DogName} is a candidate key, because the pair of columns is unique for every dog", "MicrochipNo is not a candidate key, because DogID was already chosen as the primary key", "Only the primary key is a superkey, because a superkey has to be minimal"], 0, "A superkey is any attribute set that uniquely identifies a row. A candidate key is a <i>minimal</i> superkey. {DogID, DogName} identifies rows but is not minimal, while MicrochipNo is a candidate key that simply was not chosen as the primary key."], ["<code class=\"inline\">BOARDING(<u>BoardingNo</u>, KennelNo, KennelRate)</code> has the dependency <code class=\"inline\">KennelNo &rarr; KennelRate</code>. The designer removes this transitive dependency. Which result is correct?", ["KENNEL(<u>KennelNo</u>, KennelRate) is created, and BOARDING keeps KennelNo as a foreign key", "KENNEL(<u>KennelNo</u>, KennelRate) is created, and KennelNo is deleted from BOARDING", "KENNEL(<u>KennelNo</u>, KennelRate) is created, and BOARDING keeps both KennelNo and KennelRate", "KENNEL(<u>BoardingNo</u>, KennelRate) is created, and BOARDING keeps KennelNo"], 0, "The determinant (KennelNo) becomes the primary key of the new table and must stay in the original table as a foreign key. Without it a boarding could no longer be linked to its kennel; keeping KennelRate as well would leave the redundancy in place."], ["A DSD shows <code>:boardingHandler</code> sending <code>reserveKennel(KennelNo)</code> to <code>:Kennel</code>, and then <code>:Kennel</code> sending <code>markOccupied(DogID)</code> to <code>:Dog</code>. What is wrong with the diagram?", ["The Kennel must be drawn at the top of the diagram, before the handler is shown", "Nothing: entities may call each other freely when they work on the same use case", "Entities should not call each other; the handler should send both messages itself", "The second message must be a dashed return arrow, because it goes back to the Dog"], 2, "In the three-layer DSD the controller coordinates the entities. Entities are only called by the controller."], ["The kiosk ComboBox lists kennels by name (Garden Suite, Cosy Corner, &hellip;) but <code class=\"inline\">BOARDING</code> stores the <code class=\"inline\">KennelNo</code> as a foreign key. Which binding is correct?", ["<code class=\"inline\">DisplayMember = &quot;KennelName&quot;</code>, <code class=\"inline\">ValueMember = &quot;KennelNo&quot;</code>, and read <code class=\"inline\">SelectedValue</code> when saving", "<code class=\"inline\">DisplayMember = &quot;KennelNo&quot;</code>, <code class=\"inline\">ValueMember = &quot;KennelName&quot;</code>, and read <code class=\"inline\">SelectedValue</code> when saving", "<code class=\"inline\">DisplayMember = &quot;KennelName&quot;</code> and <code class=\"inline\">ValueMember = &quot;KennelName&quot;</code>, then look up the number later", "Leave both properties empty and save the <code class=\"inline\">Text</code> the owner sees"], 0, "DisplayMember controls what the user reads, and ValueMember holds the underlying key that becomes the foreign key. Swapping them would show numbers to the user and send a name to a numeric foreign key column."], ["A programmer builds an <code class=\"inline\">OleDbConnection conn</code> and an <code class=\"inline\">OleDbCommand cmd</code> with the INSERT text, calls <code class=\"inline\">conn.Open()</code> and then <code class=\"inline\">cmd.ExecuteNonQuery()</code>, but gets an InvalidOperationException saying the connection property has not been initialised. What is missing?", ["The command needs an OleDbDataAdapter to carry the SQL text before it can be executed", "The connection must be closed before a command is executed, so Open() is the mistake", "ExecuteNonQuery() cannot run an INSERT; ExecuteReader() must be used for every statement", "The command was never linked to the connection (cmd.Connection = conn, or conn in the constructor)"], 3, "OleDbConnection is the channel to the .accdb file, and OleDbCommand holds the SQL text and parameters. A command only knows which database to use when its Connection property is set. Opening a connection elsewhere does not attach it to the command."]]}]}, {"key": "B", "title": "Section B - Interaction Design, Usability &amp; UI Scenario", "marks": 17, "color": "yellow", "time": "about 35 minutes", "parts": [{"type": "qs", "heading": "Question B - Interaction design, usability principles and UI design (17 marks)", "scenario": "PawPrint Dog Boarding has installed a self-service <b>kiosk</b> in reception on which an <b>owner</b> books a stay for a registered dog. Figure B shows version 1 of the <i>Book a Stay</i> screen. Observations from a pilot with 30 owners:<ul><li>Twelve fields, a flashing &ldquo;50% OFF GROOMING!!&rdquo; banner and three different fonts appear on one screen. The <b>Next</b> button is pale grey on a grey background.</li><li>The owner must type the dog&rsquo;s name exactly; &ldquo;rex&rdquo; is not found when the record says &ldquo;Rex&rdquo;. Regular owners must re-enter the dog, and all their details, on every visit.</li><li>Services are typed as codes separated by commas (for example <code class=\"inline\">GR,WK</code>). The meaning of the codes is printed on a poster next to the kiosk.</li><li>If the check-out date is earlier than the check-in date, a pop-up reading <b>&ldquo;Invalid input&rdquo;</b> appears on the <i>last</i> page, without saying which field is wrong.</li><li>The button that moves the owner forward is called <b>Next</b> on page 1, <b>Finish</b> on page 2 and <b>Done</b> on page 3, and it moves around the screen.</li><li>The kiosk wipes everything after 60 seconds of inactivity and there is no Back button. After <b>Done</b> the kiosk returns to a blank welcome screen with no booking number.</li></ul>", "diagram": "<div class=\"diagram-wrap wide\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">&harr; scroll sideways to see the whole diagram</div><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 720 380\" width=\"720\" height=\"380\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Figure B: Book a Stay kiosk screen, version 1\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"ao\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"720\" height=\"380\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Figure B: Book a Stay screen (version 1), owner self-service kiosk</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"36\" width=\"680\" height=\"330\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"36\" width=\"680\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">PawPrint Kiosk 1.0</text><text x=\"686\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">✕</text><rect x=\"21\" y=\"65\" width=\"678\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#ffe100\" stroke=\"#ffe100\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#c00\">50% OFF GROOMING!!  50% OFF GROOMING!!  50% OFF GROOMING!!</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"8.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">Dog</text><rect x=\"160\" y=\"106\" width=\"200\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"121\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#777\" font-style=\"italic\">type name here</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"8.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">Knl sz (1/2/3)</text><rect x=\"160\" y=\"138\" width=\"200\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">2</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"8.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">In</text><rect x=\"160\" y=\"170\" width=\"200\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"185\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#777\" font-style=\"italic\">yyyy/m/d</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"8.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">Out</text><rect x=\"160\" y=\"202\" width=\"200\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"217\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#777\" font-style=\"italic\">yyyy/m/d</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"8.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">Svc (e.g. GR,WK)</text><rect x=\"160\" y=\"234\" width=\"200\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"249\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">GR,WK</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"8.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">Type the dog's name exactly</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"8.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">1 = S, 2 = M, 3 = L (see poster)</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"283\" font-size=\"8.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">GR grooming  WK walk  TR training (see poster)</text><rect x=\"560\" y=\"300\" width=\"100\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#e4e4e4\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"610\" y=\"316\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#cfcfcf\">Next &gt;&gt;</text><rect x=\"40\" y=\"332\" width=\"300\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff0f0\" stroke=\"#d99\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"347\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#c00\">Invalid input</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"347\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#777\">Session ends in 00:12</text></svg></div>", "qs": [{"id": "B1", "marks": 9, "q": "The <i>Book a Stay</i> screen runs on a <b>touchscreen kiosk</b>. Identify <b>three (3)</b> distinct problems. For each, name the <b>Nielsen heuristic</b> it violates <b>and</b> the relevant <b>rule for mobile / touch design</b> from the course, and explain <b>one specific change</b>. Apply each answer to the case. [9]", "a": "<p><b>Marking (3 &times; 3 = 9).</b> Per problem: a Nielsen heuristic <u>and</u> a mobile / touch rule both correct &#10003;; tied to the case &#10003;; one specific change &#10003;.</p><p><i>Mobile rules:</i> provide simple navigation; make touch areas large enough; reduce clutter; make the text large enough; stick to touch controls and avoid simple web controls; keep the forms simple; observe thumb position; design for consistency.</p><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>Problem in the case</th><th>Nielsen heuristic</th><th>Mobile / touch rule</th><th>One specific change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>Twelve fields, a flashing banner and three fonts</b> on one screen.</td><td>Aesthetic and minimalist design.</td><td>Reduce clutter.</td><td>Remove the banner, use one font and show only the fields needed on each step.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Dog name typed exactly</b>; &ldquo;rex&rdquo; is not found.</td><td>Recognition rather than recall (and error prevention).</td><td>Stick to touch controls; avoid simple web controls such as free text.</td><td>A large, touchable list of the owner&rsquo;s dogs (ComboBox: DisplayMember = DogName, ValueMember = DogID).</td></tr><tr><td><b>Services typed as codes</b> (GR,WK) explained on a poster.</td><td>Match between system and the real world.</td><td>Keep the forms simple.</td><td>Large touch checkboxes showing service names (CheckedListBox).</td></tr><tr><td><b>Next, Finish, Done</b>, and the button moves.</td><td>Consistency and standards.</td><td>Design for consistency.</td><td>One label (<i>Continue</i>) in one fixed place on every page.</td></tr><tr><td><b>No Back button</b> and a 60-second wipe.</td><td>User control and freedom.</td><td>Provide simple navigation.</td><td>Add Back and Cancel and warn before the time-out, keeping the answers.</td></tr><tr><td><b>&ldquo;Invalid input&rdquo;</b> appears on the last page.</td><td>Help users recognise, diagnose and recover from errors.</td><td>Keep the forms simple (check each step as it is completed).</td><td>A message beside the field: &ldquo;Check-out date must be on or after the check-in date.&rdquo;</td></tr><tr><td><b>Regular owners re-enter</b> the dog and all details every visit.</td><td>Flexibility and efficiency of use.</td><td>Keep the forms simple.</td><td>Pre-fill the saved owner details and last-used dog for confirmation.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Illustration of one redesigned screen that applies several of these changes (not required in the answer):</p><div class=\"diagram-wrap wide\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">&harr; scroll sideways to see the whole diagram</div><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 360\" width=\"900\" height=\"360\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Redesigned Book a Stay form\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"ao\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"900\" height=\"360\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Wireframe: Book a Stay form, version 2 (model answer)</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"36\" width=\"540\" height=\"310\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"36\" width=\"540\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">PawPrint - Book a Stay</text><text x=\"546\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">✕</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Dog *</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"78\" width=\"250\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"198\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Rex (Labrador)</text><rect x=\"416\" y=\"78\" width=\"24\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"428\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">▾</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Check-in date *</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"116\" width=\"250\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"198\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">20 October 2026</text><rect x=\"416\" y=\"116\" width=\"24\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"428\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">▾</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Check-out date *</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"154\" width=\"250\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"198\" y=\"171\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">15 October 2026</text><rect x=\"416\" y=\"154\" width=\"24\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"428\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">▾</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Services</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"194\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"197\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">✓</text><text x=\"212\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Grooming (R150)</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"216\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"212\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Daily walk (R60)</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"238\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"212\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Training (R200)</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Kennel</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">Assigned by the system: Medium</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"312\" width=\"150\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" rx=\"5\"/><text x=\"265\" y=\"330\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Confirm Booking</text><rect x=\"352\" y=\"312\" width=\"90\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#f2f4f8\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" rx=\"5\"/><text x=\"397\" y=\"330\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Cancel</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0b7a3b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">ComboBox: DisplayMember = DogName</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0b7a3b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">ValueMember = DogID (FK)</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0b7a3b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">DateTimePicker, MinDate = today</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#b3261e\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Out &lt; In: ErrorProvider icon + message here</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0b7a3b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">CheckedListBox / CheckBoxes from SERVICE</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0b7a3b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">(Display = ServiceName, Value = ServiceCode)</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"327\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0b7a3b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Verb-based buttons; Cancel keeps control</text></svg></div>"}, {"id": "B2", "marks": 2, "q": "The kiosk shows only &ldquo;Invalid input&rdquo; on the last page. Distinguish <b>weak</b> validation from <b>useful</b> validation using this message, and rewrite it as a useful message for a check-out date that is earlier than the check-in date. [2]", "a": "<p><b>Weak validation:</b> a generic message, shown only after Submit, so the user must guess the field and format and entered values may be lost &#10003;. <b>Useful validation:</b> a specific message shown <u>beside the field</u>, with the format or fix visible and valid entries preserved.</p><p><b>Rewrite:</b> &ldquo;Check-out date must be on or after the check-in date.&rdquo; next to the check-out field as soon as it loses focus (ErrorProvider) &#10003;.</p>"}, {"id": "B3", "marks": 6, "q": "The <b>process of interaction design</b> involves three core activities. Name and define each activity and give one example of how PawPrint should have carried it out for the kiosk. [6]", "a": "<p><b>Marking (3 &times; 2 = 6).</b> Per activity: name and definition &#10003;; an example suited to the kiosk &#10003;. Credit a mention that the activities are repeated (iteration) and involve users throughout.</p><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>Activity</th><th>Definition (1)</th><th>Example for the kiosk (1)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>Establishing requirements</b></td><td>Finding out what the users need and agreeing usability and user-experience goals at the start.</td><td>Interview and observe owners and agree a goal such as &ldquo;an owner books a stay in under three minutes&rdquo; before building the kiosk.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Prototyping</b></td><td>Building early, cheap versions of the design so that ideas can be tried out.</td><td>A paper or clickable mock-up of the three-step booking, tried by owners before any code is written.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Evaluating</b></td><td>Testing the design with users against the agreed goals and then improving it.</td><td>The pilot with 30 owners found the problems; after redesign, test again with a new group (iteration).</td></tr></tbody></table>"}]}]}, {"key": "C", "title": "Section C - Comprehensive Case Scenario", "marks": 68, "color": "green", "time": "about 105 minutes", "parts": [{"type": "qs", "heading": "Question C1 - Database design and ERD (16 marks)", "scenario": "<b>PawPrint Dog Boarding</b> looks after dogs while their owners are away. <i>Owners</i> are identified by a system-generated OwnerID and have a name and a cell number. <i>Dogs</i> have a system-generated DogID, a name and a breed. A dog belongs to exactly one owner, an owner may register many dogs, and an owner may be registered before any dog is added. <i>Kennels</i> have a KennelNo, a size (&ldquo;small&rdquo;, &ldquo;medium&rdquo; or &ldquo;large&rdquo;) and a daily rate. A <i>boarding</i> is one stay of one dog in one kennel: it has a system-generated BoardingNo, a check-in date, a check-out date and a status (&ldquo;booked&rdquo; when created, then &ldquo;checked in&rdquo;, &ldquo;completed&rdquo; or &ldquo;overdue&rdquo;). A kennel is used by many boardings over time. <i>Services</i> (for example grooming, daily walk, training) have a ServiceCode, a name and a price. A boarding may include many services and a service may be used on many boardings; for each one the quantity (Qty) is recorded. The only user role in the system is a receptionist.", "diagram": "<div class=\"diagram-wrap wide\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">&harr; scroll sideways to see the whole diagram</div><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1330 400\" width=\"1330\" height=\"400\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Domain class diagram\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"ao\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1330\" height=\"400\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"665\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Domain class diagram: PawPrint Dog Boarding</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"50\" width=\"220\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"50\" width=\"220\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Owner</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">OwnerID</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">OwnerName</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">OwnerCell</text><rect x=\"360\" y=\"50\" width=\"210\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"360\" y=\"50\" width=\"210\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"465\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Dog</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">DogID</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">DogName</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Breed</text><rect x=\"700\" y=\"50\" width=\"210\" height=\"122\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"700\" y=\"50\" width=\"210\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"805\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Boarding</text><text x=\"710\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BoardingNo</text><text x=\"710\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">CheckInDate</text><text x=\"710\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">CheckOutDate</text><text x=\"710\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BoardingStatus</text><rect x=\"1090\" y=\"61\" width=\"210\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"1090\" y=\"61\" width=\"210\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"1195\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Service</text><text x=\"1100\" y=\"103\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ServiceCode</text><text x=\"1100\" y=\"125\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ServiceName</text><text x=\"1100\" y=\"147\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ServicePrice</text><rect x=\"700\" y=\"270\" width=\"210\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"700\" y=\"270\" width=\"210\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"805\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Kennel</text><text x=\"710\" y=\"312\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">KennelNo</text><text x=\"710\" y=\"334\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">KennelSize</text><text x=\"710\" y=\"356\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">DailyRate</text><polyline points=\"240,100 300,100 300,100 360,100\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"248\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">1..1</text><text x=\"352\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">0..*</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">owns</text><polyline points=\"570,100 635,100 635,111 700,111\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"578\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">1..1</text><text x=\"692\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">0..*</text><text x=\"635\" y=\"105.5\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">stays in</text><polyline points=\"805,270 805,221 805,221 805,172\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"813\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">1..1</text><text x=\"813\" y=\"188\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">0..*</text><text x=\"805\" y=\"237\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">houses</text><polyline points=\"910,111 1000,111 1000,111 1090,111\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"918\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">0..*</text><text x=\"1082\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">0..*</text><text x=\"1000\" y=\"127\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">includes</text><rect x=\"945\" y=\"190\" width=\"120\" height=\"78\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"945\" y=\"190\" width=\"120\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"1005\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BoardingService</text><text x=\"955\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Qty</text><line x1=\"1000\" y1=\"111\" x2=\"1000\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/></svg></div>", "qs": [{"id": "C1.1", "marks": 9, "q": "Using the domain class diagram above, draw a fully labelled <b>entity relationship diagram (ERD)</b> for the database. Include <b>all attributes</b>, primary keys, foreign keys and the cardinality of every relationship. Resolve any many-to-many relationship. Table names must be in capital letters.", "a": "<p>The many-to-many relationship between BOARDING and SERVICE is resolved with the bridge table <b>BOARDING_SERVICE</b>, which takes the primary keys of both parents (as a composite key and as foreign keys) and the attribute of the association class (Qty).</p><div class=\"diagram-wrap wide\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">&harr; scroll sideways to see the whole diagram</div><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1350 440\" width=\"1350\" height=\"440\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"ERD (model answer): PawPrint Dog Boarding\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"ao\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1350\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"675\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ERD (model answer): PawPrint Dog Boarding</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"50\" width=\"210\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"50\" width=\"210\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"125\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">OWNER</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">PK</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">OwnerID</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">OwnerName</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">OwnerCell</text><rect x=\"350\" y=\"50\" width=\"220\" height=\"122\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"350\" y=\"50\" width=\"220\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"460\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">DOG</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">PK</text><text x=\"410\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">DogID</text><text x=\"410\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">DogName</text><text x=\"410\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Breed</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">FK</text><text x=\"410\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">OwnerID</text><rect x=\"690\" y=\"50\" width=\"240\" height=\"166\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"690\" y=\"50\" width=\"240\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"810\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BOARDING</text><text x=\"698\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">PK</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BoardingNo</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">CheckInDate</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">CheckOutDate</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BoardingStatus</text><text x=\"698\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">FK</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">DogID</text><text x=\"698\" y=\"202\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">FK</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"202\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">KennelNo</text><rect x=\"1070\" y=\"50\" width=\"250\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"1070\" y=\"50\" width=\"250\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"1195\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BOARDING_SERVICE</text><text x=\"1078\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">PK,FK</text><text x=\"1130\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BoardingNo</text><text x=\"1078\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">PK,FK</text><text x=\"1130\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ServiceCode</text><text x=\"1130\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Qty</text><rect x=\"1070\" y=\"300\" width=\"250\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"1070\" y=\"300\" width=\"250\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"1195\" y=\"318\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">SERVICE</text><text x=\"1078\" y=\"342\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">PK</text><text x=\"1130\" y=\"342\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ServiceCode</text><text x=\"1130\" y=\"364\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ServiceName</text><text x=\"1130\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ServicePrice</text><rect x=\"690\" y=\"300\" width=\"240\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"690\" y=\"300\" width=\"240\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"810\" y=\"318\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">KENNEL</text><text x=\"698\" y=\"342\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">PK</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"342\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">KennelNo</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"364\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">KennelSize</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">DailyRate</text><polyline points=\"230,100 290,100 290,111 350,111\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"238\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">1..1</text><text x=\"342\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">0..*</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"105.5\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">owns</text><polyline points=\"570,111 630,111 630,133 690,133\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"578\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">1..1</text><text x=\"682\" y=\"127\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">0..*</text><text x=\"630\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">stays in</text><polyline points=\"810,300 810,258 810,258 810,216\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"818\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">1..1</text><text x=\"818\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">0..*</text><text x=\"810\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">houses</text><polyline points=\"930,133 1000,133 1000,100 1070,100\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"938\" y=\"127\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">1..1</text><text x=\"1062\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">0..*</text><text x=\"1000\" y=\"116.5\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">includes</text><polyline points=\"1195,300 1195,225 1195,225 1195,150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"1203\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">1..1</text><text x=\"1203\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">0..*</text><text x=\"1195\" y=\"241\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">is used in</text></svg></div><p><b>Marking guide</b></p><div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>Award marks for</th><th>Marks</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Six tables with correct names (OWNER, DOG, KENNEL, BOARDING, SERVICE, BOARDING_SERVICE): 5 correct = &frac12;, all six including the bridge = 2</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>All attributes present and in the correct table; no methods</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Primary keys: OwnerID, DogID, KennelNo, BoardingNo, ServiceCode; BOARDING_SERVICE composite (BoardingNo, ServiceCode)</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Foreign keys: DOG.OwnerID, BOARDING.DogID, BOARDING.KennelNo, BOARDING_SERVICE.BoardingNo, BOARDING_SERVICE.ServiceCode</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Cardinalities on all five relationships, with the 1..1 end at the parent</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td><b>Total</b></td><td><b>9</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>"}, {"id": "C1.2", "marks": 3, "q": "(a) Write the business rule, in a full sentence, that the <i>Owner&ndash;Dog</i> relationship expresses, and the one that the <i>Kennel&ndash;Boarding</i> relationship expresses. [1 each]<br>(b) Explain why the ERD needs the table BOARDING_SERVICE although the business describes only boardings and services. [1]", "a": "<p><b>(a)</b> Owner&ndash;Dog: <i>&ldquo;An owner may register many dogs (or none yet), but each dog belongs to exactly one owner.&rdquo;</i> &#10003;<br>Kennel&ndash;Boarding: <i>&ldquo;A kennel is used by many boardings over time (possibly none yet), but each boarding takes place in exactly one kennel.&rdquo;</i> &#10003;</p><p><b>(b)</b> A relational table cannot hold a many-to-many relationship directly: a boarding has many services and a service is used on many boardings. The bridge table turns it into two one-to-many relationships and is where the Qty of each service on each boarding is stored &#10003;.</p>"}, {"id": "C1.3", "marks": 4, "q": "The receptionist currently records service use in a spreadsheet. Study the sample rows below. The primary key is the <b>composite (BoardingNo, ServiceCode)</b>. The dependencies are ServiceCode &rarr; ServiceName, ServicePrice and BoardingNo &rarr; CheckInDate.<br><div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>BoardingNo</th><th>ServiceCode</th><th>ServiceName</th><th>ServicePrice</th><th>Qty</th><th>CheckInDate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>101</td><td>GR</td><td>Grooming</td><td>150</td><td>1</td><td>2026/10/05</td></tr><tr><td>101</td><td>WK</td><td>Daily walk</td><td>60</td><td>3</td><td>2026/10/05</td></tr><tr><td>102</td><td>GR</td><td>Grooming</td><td>150</td><td>2</td><td>2026/10/07</td></tr></tbody></table></div>(a) State the highest normal form the table is in. [1]<br>(b) Name the type of dependency that causes the problem. [1]<br>(c) Normalise the table to third normal form. Redraw the tables and underline the primary keys. [2]", "a": "<p><b>(a)</b> <b>1NF</b> &#10003; (all values atomic, but there are partial dependencies, so 2NF is violated).</p><p><b>(b)</b> <b>Partial dependencies</b> &#10003;: ServiceName and ServicePrice depend on ServiceCode only, and CheckInDate depends on BoardingNo only, each a part of the composite key. Only Qty depends on the whole key.</p><p><b>(c)</b> (&frac12; per table, &frac12; for keys/FKs):</p><ul><li>BOARDING (<u>BoardingNo</u>, CheckInDate)</li><li>SERVICE (<u>ServiceCode</u>, ServiceName, ServicePrice)</li><li>BOARDING_SERVICE (<u>BoardingNo, ServiceCode</u>, Qty)</li></ul><p>BoardingNo and ServiceCode in BOARDING_SERVICE are foreign keys. The price of grooming is now stored once. Each table is also in 3NF (no transitive dependencies remain).</p>"}]}, {"type": "qs", "heading": "Question C2 - Use case realisation (25 marks)", "scenario": "The following flow of activities has been developed for the <i>Create boarding</i> use case.<div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>Actor</th><th>System</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1. Requests to create boarding</td><td>1.1 Prompts for DogID, KennelNo, check-in date, check-out date and the service codes required (zero or more)</td></tr><tr><td>2. Enters DogID, KennelNo, CheckInDate, CheckOutDate and the service codes</td><td>2.1 Invokes <i>Search dog</i> use case to display the dog&rsquo;s name and owner<br><br>2.2 Uses KennelNo, CheckInDate and CheckOutDate to check whether the kennel is available (no overlapping boarding exists for those dates)<br><br><i>If the kennel is available</i><br>2.3 Receives a newly generated BoardingNo from the database management system and creates a new boarding in the BOARDING table, including BoardingNo, DogID, KennelNo, CheckInDate, CheckOutDate and BoardingStatus = &ldquo;booked&rdquo;<br><br>2.4 For each service code: uses ServiceCode to retrieve the ServiceName from the SERVICE table and creates a new BoardingService record (BoardingNo, ServiceCode, Qty = 1)<br><br>2.5 Confirms creation of the boarding and displays the BoardingNo</td></tr><tr><td><i>Extensions</i></td><td><i>If the kennel is not available</i><br>2.3 Displays &ldquo;Kennel not available for those dates&rdquo; and does not create a boarding</td></tr></tbody></table></div>", "qs": [{"id": "C2.1", "marks": 18, "q": "Draw and fully label a <b>design sequence diagram</b> (three-layer: boundary, controller and entity objects) to realise the <i>Create boarding</i> use case. Include the <b>extension</b> and any <b>interaction frames</b> you need. Objects that are created during the use case must be drawn where they are created.", "a": "<p>Model answer (any equivalent, consistently named design earns full marks; for example the new boarding may return BoardingNo as a dashed return or a variable assignment, and the kennel check may be a count of overlapping boardings sent to :Boarding):</p><div class=\"diagram-wrap wide\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">&harr; scroll sideways to see the whole diagram</div><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1525 904\" width=\"1525\" height=\"904\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Sequence Diagram: Create Boarding\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"ao\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1525\" height=\"904\" fill=\"#fff\"/><line x1=\"95\" y1=\"124\" x2=\"95\" y2=\"888\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"888\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><line x1=\"515\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"515\" y2=\"888\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><line x1=\"730\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"730\" y2=\"888\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><line x1=\"945\" y1=\"510\" x2=\"945\" y2=\"888\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><line x1=\"1160\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"1160\" y2=\"888\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><line x1=\"1375\" y1=\"668\" x2=\"1375\" y2=\"888\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><rect x=\"221.5\" y=\"56\" width=\"157\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\">:CreateBoardingForm</text><rect x=\"447\" y=\"56\" width=\"136\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"515\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\">:boardingHandler</text><rect x=\"682\" y=\"56\" width=\"96\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"730\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\">:Kennel</text><rect x=\"897\" y=\"482\" width=\"96\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"945\" y=\"500\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\">:Boarding</text><rect x=\"1112\" y=\"56\" width=\"96\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"1160\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\">:Service</text><rect x=\"1307\" y=\"640\" width=\"136\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"1375\" y=\"658\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\">:BoardingService</text><rect x=\"252\" y=\"444\" width=\"1226\" height=\"360\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><path d=\"M252 444 h42 v13 l-8 9 h-34 z\" fill=\"#eef2fa\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"258\" y=\"459\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">alt</text><text x=\"306\" y=\"460\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">[available = true]</text><line x1=\"252\" y1=\"724\" x2=\"1478\" y2=\"724\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 4\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"738\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">[available = false]</text><rect x=\"481\" y=\"562\" width=\"983\" height=\"110\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><path d=\"M481 562 h50 v13 l-8 9 h-42 z\" fill=\"#eef2fa\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"487\" y=\"577\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">loop</text><text x=\"543\" y=\"578\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">[for each service code]</text><text x=\"762.5\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Sequence Diagram: Create Boarding</text><circle cx=\"95\" cy=\"64\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><line x1=\"95\" y1=\"71\" x2=\"95\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"83\" y1=\"78\" x2=\"107\" y2=\"78\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"95\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"85\" y2=\"104\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"95\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"105\" y2=\"104\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"95\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Receptionist</text><line x1=\"95\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"298\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"197.5\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">requestCreateBoarding()</text><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"240\" x2=\"97\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" marker-end=\"url(#ao)\"/><text x=\"197.5\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">promptForDetails()</text><line x1=\"95\" y1=\"280\" x2=\"298\" y2=\"280\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"197.5\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">enterDetails(DogID, KennelNo, CheckInDate, CheckOutDate, serviceCodes)</text><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"320\" x2=\"513\" y2=\"320\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"407.5\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">createBoarding(DogID, KennelNo, CheckInDate, CheckOutDate, serviceCodes)</text><rect x=\"475\" y=\"330\" width=\"295\" height=\"34\" fill=\"#eef2fa\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><path d=\"M475 330 h34 v11 l-7 8 h-27 z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"481\" y=\"343\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ref</text><text x=\"634.5\" y=\"352\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Search dog</text><line x1=\"515\" y1=\"418\" x2=\"728\" y2=\"418\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"622.5\" y=\"412\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">available := checkAvailability(KennelNo, CheckInDate, CheckOutDate)</text><line x1=\"515\" y1=\"496\" x2=\"895\" y2=\"496\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"706\" y=\"490\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">createBoarding(DogID, KennelNo, CheckInDate, CheckOutDate, &quot;booked&quot;)</text><line x1=\"945\" y1=\"536\" x2=\"517\" y2=\"536\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" marker-end=\"url(#ao)\"/><text x=\"730\" y=\"530\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">BoardingNo</text><line x1=\"515\" y1=\"610\" x2=\"1158\" y2=\"610\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"837.5\" y=\"604\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">name := getServiceName(ServiceCode)</text><line x1=\"515\" y1=\"654\" x2=\"1305\" y2=\"654\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"911\" y=\"648\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">createBoardingService(BoardingNo, ServiceCode, 1)</text><line x1=\"515\" y1=\"712\" x2=\"302\" y2=\"712\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" marker-end=\"url(#ao)\"/><text x=\"407.5\" y=\"706\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">confirmation(BoardingNo)</text><line x1=\"515\" y1=\"786\" x2=\"302\" y2=\"786\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" marker-end=\"url(#ao)\"/><text x=\"407.5\" y=\"780\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">kennelUnavailable</text><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"844\" x2=\"97\" y2=\"844\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" marker-end=\"url(#ao)\"/><text x=\"197.5\" y=\"838\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">displayMessage(text)</text></svg></div><p><b>Marking guide</b></p><div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>Award marks for</th><th>Marks</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Notation: actor as stick figure top-left; lifelines in rectangles, prefixed with a colon and underlined; solid filled-head requests; dashed open-head returns</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Boundary <i>:CreateBoardingForm</i> and controller <i>:boardingHandler</i> both present and correctly named and placed</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Existing entities <i>:Kennel</i> and <i>:Service</i> at the top; new entities <i>:Boarding</i> and <i>:BoardingService</i> drawn lower, at their point of creation</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Actor &rarr; Form requests, Form &rarr; Handler with all parameters including the service codes</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td><b>ref</b> frame <i>Search dog</i></td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Availability check sent to :Kennel with the result returned or assigned</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>alt</b> frame with both guards ([available = true] / [available = false]) and a dashed divider</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Creation of :Boarding: arrow from the Handler pointing at the new box (not the lifeline) with the parameters including status &ldquo;booked&rdquo;; BoardingNo returned</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td><b>loop</b> frame with a guard ([for each service code]) nested in the first alt branch</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Inside the loop: the service lookup to :Service and the creation of :BoardingService</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Confirmation / unavailable returns and the final message to the actor</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Total</b></td><td><b>18</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>"}, {"id": "C2.2", "marks": 3, "q": "Write down the <b>post-conditions</b> for the <i>Create boarding</i> use case: two for a successful booking and one for the extension. [1 each]", "a": "<ul><li><b>Success 1:</b> A new BOARDING record exists with a system-generated BoardingNo, the entered DogID, KennelNo and dates, and BoardingStatus = &ldquo;booked&rdquo;. &#10003;</li><li><b>Success 2:</b> One BOARDING_SERVICE record exists for every service code that was selected, linked to the new BoardingNo. &#10003;</li><li><b>Extension (kennel unavailable):</b> No BOARDING or BOARDING_SERVICE record is created and the receptionist is told that the kennel is not available. &#10003;</li></ul>"}, {"id": "C2.3", "marks": 2, "q": "List <b>two pre-conditions</b> for the <i>Create boarding</i> use case. [1 each]", "a": "<p>Any two (&#10003; each): the receptionist is logged in; the dog is already registered (and so is its owner); the kennel exists; the service codes entered exist in the SERVICE table; the database is available.</p>"}, {"id": "C2.4", "marks": 2, "q": "The use case <i>Create boarding</i> invokes <i>Search dog</i> instead of repeating its steps. Explain why this is good design and name the relationship between the two use cases. [2]", "a": "<p>The search steps are defined once and reused by several use cases (for example Create boarding and Update dog), so a change is made in one place and the diagrams stay consistent and shorter &#10003;. The relationship is <b>&laquo;include&raquo;</b> (shown in the DSD with a ref frame) &#10003;.</p>"}]}, {"type": "qs", "heading": "Question C3 - Partial sequence diagram (8 marks)", "scenario": "Every morning the receptionist runs <i>Flag overdue boardings</i>. A boarding is <b>overdue</b> when its check-out date is earlier than today&rsquo;s date and its status is still &ldquo;checked in&rdquo;. The handler asks the BOARDING class for the list of overdue boardings for today&rsquo;s date and then sets the status of <b>each</b> boarding in that list to &ldquo;overdue&rdquo;. Study the partial sequence diagram below (the use case is started by a timer or by another use case, so there is no boundary object).", "diagram": "<div class=\"diagram-wrap wide\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">&harr; scroll sideways to see the whole diagram</div><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 810 432\" width=\"810\" height=\"432\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Partial Sequence Diagram: Flag Overdue Boardings\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"ao\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"810\" height=\"432\" fill=\"#fff\"/><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"360\" y2=\"416\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><line x1=\"660\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"660\" y2=\"416\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><rect x=\"312\" y=\"56\" width=\"96\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">(a)</tspan></text><rect x=\"612\" y=\"56\" width=\"96\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"660\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">(b)</tspan></text><rect x=\"326\" y=\"266\" width=\"368\" height=\"66\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><path d=\"M326 266 h42 v13 l-8 9 h-34 z\" fill=\"#eef2fa\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"332\" y=\"281\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">(e)</tspan></text><text x=\"380\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">(f)</tspan></text><text x=\"405\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Partial Sequence Diagram: Flag Overdue Boardings</text><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"358\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"215\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">requestFlagOverdue(<tspan font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">(c)</tspan>)</text><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"240\" x2=\"658\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"510\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">overdueList := <tspan font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">(d)</tspan></text><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"314\" x2=\"658\" y2=\"314\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"510\" y=\"308\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">(g)</tspan></text><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"372\" x2=\"72\" y2=\"372\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" marker-end=\"url(#ao)\"/><text x=\"215\" y=\"366\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">(h)</tspan></text></svg></div>", "qs": [{"id": "C3.1", "marks": 8, "q": "Supply the missing labels that correspond to (a) to (h). [1 mark each]<br><b>Note:</b> You do NOT have to redraw the sequence diagram.", "a": "<div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>Label</th><th>Answer</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>(a)</td><td><b>:boardingHandler</b></td><td>The controller that receives the request and sends every other message.</td></tr><tr><td>(b)</td><td><b>:Boarding</b></td><td>The entity that supplies the list of overdue boardings and whose status is updated.</td></tr><tr><td>(c)</td><td><b>CurrentDate</b></td><td>The parameter of the request; it is the same date passed to <i>getOverdueBoardings</i> (&ldquo;today&rsquo;s date&rdquo;).</td></tr><tr><td>(d)</td><td><b>getOverdueBoardings(CurrentDate)</b></td><td>A search message that returns a list, stored in <i>overdueList</i> (verb-noun, camelCase).</td></tr><tr><td>(e)</td><td><b>Loop</b></td><td>The same step is repeated for <b>each</b> boarding in the list, so the frame is a Loop (not Opt or Alt).</td></tr><tr><td>(f)</td><td><b>[for each boarding in overdueList]</b></td><td>The loop guard states what is iterated over, taken from the scenario.</td></tr><tr><td>(g)</td><td><b>setBoardingStatus(BoardingNo, &ldquo;overdue&rdquo;)</b></td><td>Update message from the controller to :Boarding, sent once per iteration. Accept <i>updateStatus(&ldquo;overdue&rdquo;)</i>.</td></tr><tr><td>(h)</td><td><b>confirmation</b></td><td>Dashed return to the caller after the loop has finished. Accept <i>return confirmation</i>.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><b>Completed diagram (answers in green):</b></p><div class=\"diagram-wrap wide\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">&harr; scroll sideways to see the whole diagram</div><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 810 432\" width=\"810\" height=\"432\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Partial Sequence Diagram: Flag Overdue Boardings\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"ao\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"810\" height=\"432\" fill=\"#fff\"/><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"360\" y2=\"416\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><line x1=\"660\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"660\" y2=\"416\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><rect x=\"292\" y=\"56\" width=\"136\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\"><tspan fill=\"#0b7a3b\" font-weight=\"700\">:boardingHandler</tspan></text><rect x=\"612\" y=\"56\" width=\"96\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"660\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\"><tspan fill=\"#0b7a3b\" font-weight=\"700\">:Boarding</tspan></text><rect x=\"326\" y=\"266\" width=\"368\" height=\"66\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><path d=\"M326 266 h50 v13 l-8 9 h-42 z\" fill=\"#eef2fa\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"332\" y=\"281\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\"><tspan fill=\"#0b7a3b\" font-weight=\"700\">Loop</tspan></text><text x=\"388\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\"><tspan fill=\"#0b7a3b\" font-weight=\"700\">[for each boarding in overdueList]</tspan></text><text x=\"405\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Partial Sequence Diagram: Flag Overdue Boardings</text><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"358\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"215\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">requestFlagOverdue(<tspan fill=\"#0b7a3b\" font-weight=\"700\">CurrentDate</tspan>)</text><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"240\" x2=\"658\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"510\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">overdueList := <tspan fill=\"#0b7a3b\" font-weight=\"700\">getOverdueBoardings(CurrentDate)</tspan></text><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"314\" x2=\"658\" y2=\"314\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"510\" y=\"308\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><tspan fill=\"#0b7a3b\" font-weight=\"700\">setBoardingStatus(BoardingNo, &quot;overdue&quot;)</tspan></text><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"372\" x2=\"72\" y2=\"372\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" marker-end=\"url(#ao)\"/><text x=\"215\" y=\"366\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><tspan fill=\"#0b7a3b\" font-weight=\"700\">confirmation</tspan></text></svg></div>"}]}, {"type": "qs", "heading": "Question C4 - ADO.NET code analysis (7 marks)", "scenario": "The <i>BoardingHandler</i> contains the method below. BOARDING 101 exists, and the tables hold the rows shown. ServicePrice is a whole number (Long Integer) and (BoardingNo, ServiceCode) is the primary key of BOARDING_SERVICE.<div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>ServiceCode</th><th>ServiceName</th><th>ServicePrice</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>GR</td><td>Grooming</td><td>150</td></tr><tr><td>WK</td><td>Daily walk</td><td>60</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>BoardingNo</th><th>ServiceCode</th><th>Qty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>101</td><td>GR</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><pre class=\"sql\">public string addService(int boardingNo, string serviceCode, int qty)\n{\n    string msg = &quot;&quot;;\n    OleDbConnection conn = new OleDbConnection(connString);\n    try\n    {\n        conn.Open();\n        OleDbCommand chk = new OleDbCommand(\n          &quot;SELECT ServicePrice FROM SERVICE WHERE ServiceCode = ?&quot;, conn);\n        chk.Parameters.AddWithValue(&quot;?&quot;, serviceCode);\n        object price = chk.ExecuteScalar();\n        if (price == null) return &quot;No such service&quot;;\n\n        OleDbCommand ins = new OleDbCommand(\n          &quot;INSERT INTO BOARDING_SERVICE (BoardingNo, ServiceCode, Qty) VALUES (?, ?, ?)&quot;, conn);\n        ins.Parameters.AddWithValue(&quot;?&quot;, boardingNo);\n        ins.Parameters.AddWithValue(&quot;?&quot;, serviceCode);\n        ins.Parameters.AddWithValue(&quot;?&quot;, qty);\n        int rows = ins.ExecuteNonQuery();\n        msg = rows + &quot; row added, total R&quot; + ((int)price * qty);\n    }\n    catch (OleDbException) { msg = &quot;Already added&quot;; }\n    finally { conn.Close(); }\n    return msg;\n}</pre>", "qs": [{"id": "C4.1", "marks": 2, "q": "State the exact string returned by <code class=\"inline\">addService(101, \"WK\", 3)</code>.", "a": "<p>ExecuteScalar returns 60 (boxed), so price is not null &#10003;. The INSERT adds one row, so <code class=\"inline\">rows = 1</code>. Total = 60 &times; 3 = 180. Result: <b>&ldquo;1 row added, total R180&rdquo;</b> &#10003;.</p>"}, {"id": "C4.2", "marks": 1, "q": "State the exact string returned by <code class=\"inline\">addService(101, \"XX\", 1)</code>, and say whether the connection is closed.", "a": "<p>No row matches &ldquo;XX&rdquo;, so ExecuteScalar returns <code class=\"inline\">null</code> and the method returns <b>&ldquo;No such service&rdquo;</b> from inside the try block &#10003;. The <code class=\"inline\">finally</code> block still runs, so the connection is closed.</p>"}, {"id": "C4.3", "marks": 2, "q": "State the exact string returned by <code class=\"inline\">addService(101, \"GR\", 1)</code> and explain why.", "a": "<p><b>&ldquo;Already added&rdquo;</b> &#10003;. The price lookup succeeds (150), but the row (101, GR) already exists, so the INSERT breaks the composite primary key. The DBMS rejects it, <code class=\"inline\">ExecuteNonQuery()</code> throws an <code class=\"inline\">OleDbException</code> and the catch block sets the message &#10003;.</p>"}, {"id": "C4.4", "marks": 2, "q": "A programmer adds the three INSERT parameters in the order <code class=\"inline\">serviceCode, boardingNo, qty</code>. What happens when <code class=\"inline\">addService(101, \"WK\", 3)</code> is called, and why? [2]", "a": "<p>OleDb matches parameters by <b>position</b>, not by name, so &ldquo;WK&rdquo; is sent to the BoardingNo column and 101 to ServiceCode &#10003;. A text value cannot be stored in a numeric column (data type mismatch), so an OleDbException is thrown, no row is inserted and the method returns the misleading message &ldquo;Already added&rdquo; &#10003;.</p>"}]}, {"type": "qs", "heading": "Question C5 - Report design (12 marks)", "scenario": "Operations Manager <i>Lerato Dube</i> wants to know, each month, which kennels earn the most and how well they are being used, so that she can decide where to invest and how to set the daily rates. Refer to the scenario and the domain class diagram in Question C1.", "qs": [{"id": "C5.1", "marks": 7, "q": "Use the following table to suggest a report that would be useful to the manager described above. <b>Note:</b> redraw the table in your answer book.<div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"paper-tbl\"><tbody><tr><td>Report name:</td><td>(&frac12; mark)</td></tr><tr><td>Report type:</td><td>(&frac12; mark)</td></tr><tr><td>Report format:</td><td>(&frac12; mark)</td></tr><tr><td>Report recipient(s):</td><td>(&frac12; mark)</td></tr><tr><td>Report frequency:</td><td>(&frac12; mark)</td></tr><tr><td>Report rationale:</td><td>(2 marks)</td></tr><tr><td>Decision(s) made as a result of the report:</td><td>(2&frac12; marks)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>", "a": "<p><b>One possible answer</b> (any other reasonable answer is acceptable):</p><div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"ans-table\"><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Report name</td><td>Kennel Utilisation and Revenue by Month</td></tr><tr><td>Report type</td><td>Summary / management report (aggregates stays, nights and revenue per kennel)</td></tr><tr><td>Report format</td><td>Summary table grouped by kennel and sorted by revenue; optional bar chart of revenue; on screen with PDF / print option</td></tr><tr><td>Report recipient(s)</td><td>Operations Manager (copy to the Owner of PawPrint)</td></tr><tr><td>Report frequency</td><td>Monthly, on the first working day of the next month</td></tr><tr><td>Report rationale</td><td>Shows, for each kennel, the number of stays, nights booked, revenue and occupancy (derived), so the manager can see which kennels earn the most and which stand empty without adding up individual boardings by hand.</td></tr><tr><td>Decision(s) made as a result of the report</td><td><ul><li>Whether to raise or lower the daily rate of under-used or over-demanded kennel sizes</li><li>Whether to add kennels of the most profitable size or convert unused ones</li><li>Which kennels to schedule for maintenance in quiet periods</li><li>Whether to run promotions for low-occupancy months</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Marking: &frac12; each for name, type, format, recipient and frequency; 2 for a rationale that names the problem and the data shown; 2&frac12; for decisions that are concrete actions.</p>"}, {"id": "C5.2", "marks": 3, "q": "Draw a rough <b>prototype</b> of the report you designed in C5.1. It must show a title, the reporting period, column headings with <b>sample data</b>, <b>derived fields</b> and a totals line. [3]", "a": "<div class=\"diagram-wrap wide\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">&harr; scroll sideways to see the whole diagram</div><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 400\" width=\"900\" height=\"400\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Report prototype: Kennel Utilisation and Revenue\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"ao\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"900\" height=\"400\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Report prototype (model answer)</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"34\" width=\"860\" height=\"350\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"450\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">KENNEL UTILISATION AND REVENUE</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Month: September 2026</text><text x=\"450\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Run date: 01/10/2026</text><text x=\"860\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">For: Operations Manager</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"98\" width=\"840\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Kennel</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Size</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Stays</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Nights</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Daily Rate</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Revenue</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Occupancy %</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"124\" width=\"840\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#bbb\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">K03</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Large</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">3</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">19</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">R300</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">R5 700</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">63%</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"150\" width=\"840\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#bbb\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">K02</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Medium</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">5</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">24</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">R220</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">R5 280</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">80%</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"176\" width=\"840\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#bbb\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">K01</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Small</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">6</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">28</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">R180</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">R5 040</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">93%</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">...</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"296\" x2=\"870\" y2=\"296\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">TOTAL</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">14</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">71</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">R16 020</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"350\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\">Sorted by Revenue (highest first).  Nights = CheckOutDate - CheckInDate;  Revenue = Nights x DailyRate;  Occupancy % = Nights / 30</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"368\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\">[derived fields: not stored in the database]</text></svg></div><p><b>Marking guide</b></p><div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>Award marks for</th><th>Marks</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Header block: title, period / run date, recipient</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Body: relevant columns with realistic sample rows, grouped / sorted</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Derived fields (Nights, Revenue, Occupancy %) and a totals line</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Total</b></td><td><b>3</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>"}, {"id": "C5.3", "marks": 2, "q": "Write the SQL query that would supply the data for your report. [2]", "a": "<pre class=\"sql\">SELECT k.KennelNo, k.KennelSize,\n       COUNT(b.BoardingNo) AS Stays,\n       SUM(DateDiff(&quot;d&quot;, b.CheckInDate, b.CheckOutDate)) AS Nights,\n       SUM(DateDiff(&quot;d&quot;, b.CheckInDate, b.CheckOutDate) * k.DailyRate) AS Revenue\nFROM KENNEL AS k INNER JOIN BOARDING AS b ON k.KennelNo = b.KennelNo\nWHERE b.CheckInDate &gt;= #2026-09-01# AND b.CheckInDate &lt; #2026-10-01#\nGROUP BY k.KennelNo, k.KennelSize\nORDER BY SUM(DateDiff(&quot;d&quot;, b.CheckInDate, b.CheckOutDate) * k.DailyRate) DESC;</pre><p>&#10003; Correct join of KENNEL to BOARDING on KennelNo with the date range for the month. &#10003; <code class=\"inline\">GROUP BY</code> on the non-aggregated columns with COUNT / SUM and the derived revenue calculation (and an ORDER BY). The comma-join with a WHERE condition is also accepted.</p>"}]}]}]};